<div class="docs">
    <div class="page-head">
        <div>
            <h1 class="page-title">Integration docs</h1>
            <p class="page-sub">Connect the loader and mod with one call.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-actions"><a href="/api-docs" class="btn btn-secondary">{{icon "book-open"}}API docs</a></div>
    </div>
    {{> msgStatus}}
    <section class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
            <div class="tile teal">{{icon "plug-zap"}}</div>
            <div><h2 class="card-title">Overview</h2></div>
        </div>
        <p class="muted">Loader / mod integration: one call does everything —
        <span class="doc-inline">POST /connect</span>. Below is the connect URL, every response field
        (mod name, status text, floating text, mod features, expiry), the error text, and simple C++ code.
        The full reference also lives in <span class="doc-inline">INTEGRATION.md</span> in the repo.</p>
        <p class="doc-note" style="margin-top:14px">Need to <strong>create, list or delete licence keys</strong> from your
        own site or Telegram bot? That is a different API with personal API keys — see
        <a href="/api-keys">API keys</a> and <a href="/api-docs">API docs (key management)</a>.
        This page is only for the loader / mod side.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>Base URL</h2>
            <code class="doc-url">{{apiBase}}</code>
            <p>Every endpoint below is relative to this host. All loader traffic must use HTTPS.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>1. Connect URL</h2>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>POST {{apiBase}}/connect
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

game=PUBG&amp;user_key=ANOY-2H-LYK0Y&amp;serial=DEVICE123</code></pre>
            <p>GET is also supported for loaders that use a query string:
            <span class="doc-inline">/connect?game=PUBG&amp;user_key=…&amp;serial=…</span>.
            <span class="doc-inline">/api/connect</span> is an alias.</p>
            <div class="table-scroll">
                <table class="responsive">
                    <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Rules</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">game</span></td><td>required, letters / digits / <span class="doc-inline">_</span> / <span class="doc-inline">-</span></td><td>Game the key was generated for (default <span class="doc-inline">PUBG</span>)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">user_key</span></td><td>required, 1–36 characters</td><td>Licence key from <span class="doc-inline">/keys</span></td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">serial</span></td><td>required, letters / digits / <span class="doc-inline">_</span> / <span class="doc-inline">-</span></td><td>Stable per-device ID; stored against the key</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>2. curl example</h2>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>curl -sS -X POST {{apiBase}}/connect \
  -d 'game=PUBG' \
  -d 'user_key=ANOY-2H-LYK0Y' \
  -d 'serial=DEVICE123'</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>3. Success response</h2>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>{
  "status": true,
  "data": {
    "real": "PUBG-ANOY-2H-LYK0Y-DEVICE123-STATIC_WORDS",
    "token": "1aa36c890b3155533de4ed2e09714704",
    "modname": "VIP MOD",
    "mod_status": "Safe",
    "credit": "MOD STATUS :- 100% SAFE",
    "ESP": "on", "Item": "on", "AIM": "on", "SilentAim": "on",
    "BulletTrack": "on", "Floating": "on", "Memory": "on", "Setting": "on",
    "expired_date": "2026-11-05T11:00:20.704Z",
    "EXP": "2026-11-05T11:00:20.704Z",
    "exdate": "2026-11-05T11:00:20.704Z",
    "device": 1,
    "rng": 1762333220
  }
}</code></pre>
            <p>Always check <span class="doc-inline">status</span> first. Maintenance mode also returns
            <span class="doc-inline">status:true</span> but has <strong>no</strong> <span class="doc-inline">data</span> object — only a
            <span class="doc-inline">reason</span> message. Treat that as not authorised.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>4. Response fields</h2>
            <div class="table-scroll">
                <table class="responsive">
                    <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning / how to use it</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">status</span></td><td><span class="doc-inline">true</span> = authorised. On <span class="doc-inline">false</span>, read <span class="doc-inline">reason</span>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">reason</span></td><td>Only on failure or maintenance. See the error table below.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.real</span></td><td><span class="doc-inline">game-user_key-serial-STATIC_WORDS</span>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.token</span></td><td><span class="doc-inline">md5(real)</span>. Recompute to detect a tampered reply.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.modname</span></td><td>Mod name for your menu / title. Set at <span class="doc-inline">/Server → Change Mod Name</span>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.mod_status</span></td><td><strong>Status text</strong>: <span class="doc-inline">Safe</span> or <span class="doc-inline">Anti-Cheat is High..!!</span>. Show as a badge.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.credit</span></td><td><strong>Floating text</strong>: free-form line drawn over the mod menu, e.g. <span class="doc-inline">MOD STATUS :- 100% SAFE</span>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.ESP … Setting</span></td><td>Eight <strong>mod feature</strong> gates. Values are the strings <span class="doc-inline">"on"</span> / <span class="doc-inline">"off"</span> — not booleans. Toggled at <span class="doc-inline">/Server → Mod Features</span>.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.expired_date</span></td><td><strong>Expiry</strong> as ISO-8601 UTC. Compare with current UTC time before enabling features.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.EXP</span>, <span class="doc-inline">data.exdate</span></td><td>Same expiry value, kept for legacy loaders.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.device</span></td><td>Maximum devices allowed for this key.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">data.rng</span></td><td>Unix timestamp (seconds) when the server built the reply — anti-replay heuristic.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>5. Expiry &amp; devices</h2>
            <p>A new key has no expiry. The <strong>first successful</strong> connect sets it to
            <span class="doc-inline">now + duration hours</span> (2, 5, 24, 72, 168, 336 or 720 hours,
            chosen when the key is generated). After that it never moves and later calls return
            <span class="doc-inline">EXPIRED KEY</span>. The key's <span class="doc-inline">device</span> limit counts
            distinct serials; re-using the same serial is always allowed.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>6. Status / error text</h2>
            <p>All rejections are HTTP 200 with <span class="doc-inline">status:false</span>:</p>
            <div class="table-scroll">
                <table class="responsive">
                    <thead><tr><th>reason</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">INVALID PARAMETER</span></td><td>A parameter is missing or empty</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">Bad Parameter</span></td><td>Illegal characters or key longer than 36 chars</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">USER OR GAME NOT REGISTERED</span></td><td>Key missing, or game does not match</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">USER BLOCKED</span></td><td>Key is not active</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">EXPIRED KEY</span></td><td>Expiry time is in the past</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><span class="doc-inline">MAX DEVICE REACHED</span></td><td>New serial and the device limit is full</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>maintenance message</td><td><span class="doc-inline">status:true</span>, no <span class="doc-inline">data</span>. Show the message from <span class="doc-inline">/Server → Offline Message</span>.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>7. Use in C++</h2>
            <p>Minimal libcurl POST — no JSON library needed to see the raw reply:</p>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>// g++ connect.cpp -o connect -lcurl
#include &lt;curl/curl.h&gt;
#include &lt;iostream&gt;
#include &lt;string&gt;

static size_t onData(char* p, size_t size, size_t nmemb, void* out) {
    static_cast&lt;std::string*&gt;(out)-&gt;append(p, size * nmemb);
    return size * nmemb;
}

std::string post(const std::string&amp; url, const std::string&amp; body) {
    CURL* c = curl_easy_init();
    std::string out;
    curl_easy_setopt(c, CURLOPT_URL, url.c_str());
    curl_easy_setopt(c, CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS, body.c_str());
    curl_easy_setopt(c, CURLOPT_WRITEFUNCTION, onData);
    curl_easy_setopt(c, CURLOPT_WRITEDATA, &amp;out);
    curl_easy_setopt(c, CURLOPT_TIMEOUT, 15L);
    CURLcode rc = curl_easy_perform(c);
    if (rc != CURLE_OK) std::cerr &lt;&lt; curl_easy_strerror(rc) &lt;&lt; std::endl;
    curl_easy_cleanup(c);
    return out;
}

int main() {
    std::string json = post("{{apiBase}}/connect",
        "game=PUBG&amp;user_key=ANOY-2H-LYK0Y&amp;serial=DEVICE123");
    std::cout &lt;&lt; json &lt;&lt; std::endl;
}</code></pre>
            <p>Then parse it (example with <span class="doc-inline">nlohmann/json</span>):</p>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>#include &lt;nlohmann/json.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;string&gt;

void apply(const std::string&amp; json) {
    auto r = nlohmann::json::parse(json, nullptr, false);
    if (r.is_discarded()) return;               // bad JSON

    if (!r.value("status", false)) {
        ShowMessage(r.value("reason", "UNKNOWN ERROR"));  // EXPIRED KEY, USER BLOCKED ...
        return;
    }
    if (!r.contains("data")) {                  // maintenance mode
        ShowMessage(r.value("reason", "Server is Under Maintenance"));
        return;
    }

    const auto&amp; d = r["data"];
    std::string modName  = d.value("modname", "");       // "VIP MOD"
    std::string status   = d.value("mod_status", "");    // "Safe" / "Anti-Cheat is High..!!"
    std::string floating = d.value("credit", "");        // floating text
    std::string expiry   = d.value("expired_date", "");  // ISO-8601 UTC
    int maxDevices       = d.value("device", 1);
    std::string token    = d.value("token", "");

    bool esp       = d.value("ESP", "off") == "on";
    bool aim       = d.value("AIM", "off") == "on";
    bool silentAim = d.value("SilentAim", "off") == "on";
    bool bullet    = d.value("BulletTrack", "off") == "on";
    bool item      = d.value("Item", "off") == "on";
    bool floatingW = d.value("Floating", "off") == "on";
    bool memory    = d.value("Memory", "off") == "on";
    bool setting   = d.value("Setting", "off") == "on";

    SetMenuTitle(modName);
    DrawFloatingText(floating);
    DrawStatusBadge(status);
    EnableFeatures(esp, aim, silentAim, bullet, item, floatingW, memory, setting);
    // verify token == md5(game + "-" + key + "-" + serial + "-" + STATIC_WORDS)
    // and compare expiry with current UTC time before starting the mod.
}</code></pre>
            <p class="doc-note">The <span class="doc-inline">ShowMessage</span>, <span class="doc-inline">DrawFloatingText</span>
            and <span class="doc-inline">EnableFeatures</span> calls are placeholders for your own UI/hooks —
            the API itself is just JSON over HTTPS.</p>
        </div>

